==========   rescue-ramfs - Tools for creating a minimal recovery initramfs   ==========

HOW TO USE:
 1. # ./download-ramfs
 2. # ./chroot build musl
 3. # ./chroot build busybox
 4. # ./chroot build efibootmgr
 5. # ./chroot build e2fsprogs
 6. # ./chroot build wpa_supplicant
 7. # ./copy-keys  (copies host ssh private keys)
 8. # ./chroot build dropbear
 9. $ ./set-passwd (sets the root password for the initramfs)
10. $ ./copy-firmware
11. # ./gen-wificonf
12. Edit the variables in conf/netsetup to reflect your own settings.
13. Edit the ESP variable in conf/init to contain the location of your EFI System
    Partition.
14. # ./chroot build ramfs
15. Edit reboot-ramfs to suit your preferences and reboot:
    # ./reboot-ramfs

After running './chroot build busybox' once, you may configure busybox by running:
 # ./chroot build busybox configure

Once you are booted into the initramfs, you should be able to ssh into your
machine as you normally do.


REQUIREMENTS
You need to have minisign installed. You also need the Void release keys. On a Void
Linux system, these can be obtained by installing void-release-keys. For obtaining
the keys on a non-Void system, please consult:
 https://docs.voidlinux.org/installation/index.html#verifying-digital-signature


BUILD DURATIONS
These values were recorded on a low-spec potato from 2018. Your own build durations
will most certainly be shorter than these.

	musl				21 min
	busybox				31 s (excluding time to download archive)
	efibootmgr			22 s
	e2fsprogs			24 s
	wpa_supplicant		55 s
	dropbear			41 s
